      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T10:52:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But these aren\u0027t C `#include`s where it\u0027s all-or-nothing; `use` cherry-picks the item out of the file: `main()` makes use of `entry::RebootReason` and `entry::main_wrapper()` calls `main()` so no circular dependency? Are you saying you can\u0027t get it to compile?\n\nAFAIK, error types are typically declared within their \"use-case\" module and not grouped in a separate, dedicated module such as `errors`. If you _really_ wanted to move `RebootReason` to its own module, knowing that it won\u0027t contain any other type, why not name the module itself accordingly (e.g. \"`reboot_reason`\")?",
